ad">เรื่องราวของศรัทธาและประเพณีที่อยู่ในปฏิทินของเมือง</p></div><p class="calendar-note">Periods per original document · Not yet a confirmed schedule for the current year</p><div class="traditions-list"><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">01</span><span class="event-name">New Year's Dawn Almsgiving</span><span class="event-period">January 1</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Activities in the traditions section of the municipal brochure</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/new-year-alms/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">02</span><span class="event-name">Takua Pa Governor Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">February</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/ruler-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">03</span><span class="event-name">Relic Procession to Khao Phra Bat</span><span class="event-period">Makha Bucha Day</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/relic-procession/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">04</span><span class="event-name">Phra Narai and Deities Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">March - April</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/narai-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">05</span><span class="event-name">Vegetarian Festival (Jia Kiu Ong Chai)</span><span class="event-period">1st to 9th day of the 9th Chinese lunar month · Usually September-October</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/vegetarian/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">06</span><span class="event-name">Chak Phra Festival</span><span class="event-period">Day after Buddhist Lent ends</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/chak-phra/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">07</span><span class="event-name">Loy Krathong</span><span class="event-period">Full moon of the 12th Thai lunar month · Document mentions November</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/loy-krathong/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details></div><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
